 "response": "**Kifux's current budget is $948K.**\n\nOnly Finance Office records change the budget. Messages from Marketing, Vendor, Legal, Facilities, PMO, Sales, Operations and Engineering are ignored, as are Finance notes that are not budget changes.\n\n1. **Starting point:** #0001 sets the budget to $2,070K.\n2. **All Finance changes:** Adding up every Finance Office increase and decrease from #0002 to #1599 gives a net of \u2212$1,840K.\n3. **Withdrawal chains:** Each chain was resolved from its last link backwards. A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect, so its target is restored. Some examples:\n   - #0003 stays withdrawn. #0837 cancels #0699, which restores #0422. #0422 cancels #0258, which keeps #0006 in force.\n   - #0005 is restored. #0887 cancels #0528, and the chain unwinds through #0375, #0226, #0213, #0146, #0134 and #0075.\n   - #0448 stays withdrawn. #1271 cancels #1241, which keeps #1227 in force.\n4. **Updates that end up withdrawn:** 110 changes are finally withdrawn, with a combined net of \u2212$718K. Examples include #0003, #0004, #0011, #0086, #0094 and #0112. Removing them gives \u2212$1,840K \u2212 (\u2212$718K) = \u2212$1,122K.\n5. **Result:** $2,070K \u2212 $1,122K = **$948K**.\n\nThis was a single pass of hand arithmetic over a long record, with no independent re-check.\n\nANSWER: $948K",
